      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2229740158,
          "type": null,
          "body": "xz is a bit easier for our tooling still in Gentoo. But I got curious about the sizes.\n\nUsing `xz -9e` (the equivalent of these options for zstd), I get:\n```\n$ ls -hal wireshark-4.4.2.tar*\n-rw-r--r-- 1 sam sam 312M Nov 27 06:29 wireshark-4.4.2.tar\n-rw-r--r-- 1 sam sam  43M Nov 27 06:29 wireshark-4.4.2.tar.xz\n-rw-r--r-- 1 sam sam  44M Nov 27 06:29 wireshark-4.4.2.tar.zst\n\n$ ls -al wireshark-4.4.2.tar*\n-rw-r--r-- 1 sam sam 326983680 Nov 27 06:29 wireshark-4.4.2.tar\n-rw-r--r-- 1 sam sam  44743972 Nov 27 06:29 wireshark-4.4.2.tar.xz\n-rw-r--r-- 1 sam sam  45992118 Nov 27 06:29 wireshark-4.4.2.tar.zst\n```\nwhich is about what I expected. What numbers were you seeing?",
          "author": {
            "id": 4694399,
            "username": "thesamesam",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Sam James",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9843a18faabed3a1bef94c9e8099ecb78b655e7870246913e2e8278d169a69b8?s=80&d=identicon",
